{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376293-has-anyone-utilized-the-strix-as-playable-characters","id":1376293,"title":"Has Anyone utilized the Strix as playable characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-23T12:49:55-07:00","id":1376293,"title":"Has Anyone utilized the Strix as playable characters?","content":"This is just my two cents but I think that playing as inmortal owl protovampires who poseses stuff is as fun as it sounds but at least the impresion that I get from them is that they are too antagonistic with all the I hate you for having born with a skin suit , how dare you!?.<br /> <br /> Instead why not make them Apex Predators who make devilish deals with kindred not becuase they are antagonistic to them as a whole but becuase they can get with it thanks to their powers , in reality they just want to do what an inteligent beast would , Feed , Reproduce and Dominate their competition that being the reason why they are so arrogant at times.What happened in Rome? , well what did you expect breaking a deal with them it would damage their reputation if vengance where not to be exerted , this of course makes vampires really wary of them and rightfully so becuase they are not their friends just bussiness partners who would like to enslave them or kill them and steal their domain but who know how to be midly polite if they don\u00b4t have an assured victory.\u00bfAre they really that different from other vampires?<br /> <br /> Of course the rightly placed fear of them would be the reason why they don\u00b4t announce themselves to other vampires as Strix prefering to act with skin suits unless they know they can get away with their devilish deals , why figh them directly if you can posses the prince or their children and kill them while sleeping? Of course there are strix who like to play with their prey be them humans or vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Some Changes I have been thinking for the Strix to be more player friendly:</b><ul><li>Strix take half the &quot;Aggravated damage&quot; their possesed bodies take.</li> <li>Strix are invulnerable to superficial damage but lethal now harms them as bashing , agg damage acts doesnt get nerfed.</li> <li>Strix would be able to heal damage expending vitae and they would feed and hunt vitae from other vampires or from humans if they have possesed a vampire.</li> <li>They can vampirize a body and teach it disciplines (that way losing a body in wich you have invested means a defeat)</li> <li>As a last resort Strix would be able to go back to the crepuscular zone but for each strix that wants to manifest there need to be at least 5 vampires on the city (They do not want to exterminate vampires , only the alpha ones to take their seats).</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 03-24-2020, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T19:36:36-07:00","id":1376358,"title":"","content":"I dont believe strix will ever be playable in an even semi-traditional sense. <br /> <br /> The Strix are above the Kindred, or so they claim. They hate vampires for any number of reasons, many of them being they find them holding to their humanity annoying.<br /> <br /> Moreover, they serve as antagonists due to their very dealings with the Kindred. Whether they are preying on them, making deals with them as you said, or treating the masquerade as a total joke, the Strix exists to ruin the all night society. They arent meant to be sympathetic, they arent meant to be in sync with the Kindred, and they arent meant to a fairly easy issue for vampires to overcome.<br /> <br /> They arent playable and likely never will be. If they were, they would make for horribly flat player characters. And I do think there was a thread like this very long ago that went the same way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T22:17:04-07:00","id":1376370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376293-has-anyone-utilized-the-strix-as-playable-characters#post1376293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">superficial damage</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T03:16:11-07:00","id":1376386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376293-has-anyone-utilized-the-strix-as-playable-characters?p=1376370#post1376370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bashing Damage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T15:02:35-07:00","id":1376440,"title":"","content":"I think one of the sticking points is that using the Strix adds a lot of baggage to the fun that could be explored. The Strix specific stuff isn't what makes a case for there to be something worth exploring in game play.<br /> <br /> Like, what about a micro-template of mortals with some wish-granting entity bonded to them? The mortal gets extended life and some other perks, but has to feed the wish-granting-thing regularly or bad stuff happens. There's plenty of stories about mysterious folks offering strange deals to base it on. You're not stuck with vampires so you can explore more things; Demons and the Lost are obvious splats to have interesting conflicts with. <br /> <br /> And a big deal is that it lets you start lower, and start with lower stakes instead of right to the top of conflicts with vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T18:53:57-07:00","id":1376465,"title":"","content":"I played around with rules for playable Strix at one point, refactoring their Dread Powers and Manifestations into a series of Discipline-like tracks independent of Shadow Potency. I think the concept certainly has some potential!<br /> <br /> The difficulty is, as others have said, playing something that is not human and never was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T22:43:40-07:00","id":1376659,"title":"","content":"So this is my thought process. The basic premise of being an incoporial vampire who possesses bodies doesn't sound bad. The issue I run into is what do you care about? <br /> <br /> I think the big problem with playing a strix as-is is that they don't care about anything that is fun to rp for a extended period of time. Like, broadly, you've got experience junkies, murder hobos, and stalkers who want to ruin your life.<br /> <br /> The only thing that seems like it would be remotely interesting for a story would be the stalkers. But there's nothing to dig into there. /I wanna ruin that dude's life/. Why? /Because fuck them/. <br /> <br /> Most of your tension in a Vampire game comes from &quot;I want a think that's difficult to get, and the easiest way is through terrible means.&quot; But that implies that you have two desires in conflict - your overall goal and your desire to remain moral. <br /> <br /> So change the fluff. They aren't evil hate demons. Maybe they're legitimately wronged ghosts, who only want to hurt one particular person. Or, like the Hollow Mekhet reflections, they want revenge but their survival is contingent on the continued survival of the target of their victim. <br /> <br /> This is how I'd do it. I'd make them incoporial ghosts who want to live again, but nonconsentual possession results in loss of Shadow Potency. So now they need to deal with their hosts wants, and they can't just go around hijacking bodies willy nilly. Either possession still harms the living, or hosts are able to potentially eject posessors. If they can't eject the strix, then make the vampires aware of the striges reputation as liars. <br /> <br /> <br /> You need to make consequences matter, and you do that by giving the characters something to care about. The more things they care about, and the easier they conflict, the more drama you get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 03-26-2020, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}